WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
- So I have a question.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.790
If you owe a billion dollars,

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.930
are you a billionaire?

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.030
Now, sure, Alex Jones
has been ordered to pay

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.440
close to a billion dollars,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.600
but this is great news for Alex Jones.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.940
He's finally going to
get that real bankruptcy

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.170
that he's been angling for

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.549
for all this time.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:16.890
- [Judge] Total of $120 million.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.630
- Yeah!
- Initialed by juror-

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:19.800
- And that's because a Connecticut jury

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.660
has found that Jones and
Infowars should pay $965 million

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.670
to people who've suffered
from his false claim

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.490
that the Sandy Hook Elementary
school shooting was a hoax.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:31.830
Robbie Parker, the father of a
six year old girl named Emily

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.630
who was murdered that day, said, quote,

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.130
- All I can really say is
that I'm just proud that

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.270
what we were able to accomplish was just

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.250
to simply tell the truth,

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.810
and it shouldn't be this hard,

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.580
and it shouldn't be this scary.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.920
- While Parker gave his
heartbreaking statements,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.720
Jones was live on Infowars,

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.280
calling the verdict hilarious.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.113
Telling his audience

00:00:51.113 --> 00:00:53.430
that he'd never pay these
people a single penny,

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.560
and asked his fan base for donations,

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.550
because,

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.383
of course.

00:00:57.383 --> 00:00:58.650
So the real question is,

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.610
will this Info-hole finally
have to pay up, or what?

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.470
Now, here's the background on this case.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.420
The Connecticut verdict
is right on the heels

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.530
of a Texas jury verdict

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.150
awarding millions of
dollars to the parents

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.130
of other children killed in the massacre.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.040
In both cases, Jones did not
defend the case on the merits,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.440
and the courts entered
default judgments against him

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.070
because of all kinds of
shenanigans on Jones' part.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.050
He effectively refused to comply

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.820
with discovery in all of these cases.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.040
The lawsuit stems from Infowars' broadcast

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.830
about the shooting at Sandy
Hook Elementary School in 2012

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:30.870
that killed 20 first grade children,

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.090
six educators, and wounded two others.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.220
The plaintiffs included the
relatives of five children,

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.140
and three educators killed
in the mass shooting,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.490
plus an FBI agent

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.620
who was one of the first
responders to the scene.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.120
As the plaintiffs in
this case pointed out,

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.220
quote, "Overwhelming and
indisputable evidence

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.900
shows exactly what happened

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.200
at Sandy Hook Elementary
School on December 14th, 2012.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.300
26 children and educators were shot

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.060
by a lone youth, armed with an AR-15.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.260
Now, despite all of the evidence

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.270
that 26 people lost their lives that day,

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.310
Jones' broadcast lies about Sandy Hook

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.420
for over five years on
his Infowars news program.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.610
Jones and Infowars contributors said

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.140
that the entire thing was a hoax

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.820
staged by the government,

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.920
in order to take away the audience's guns.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.637
Jones and his contributors
said things like,

00:02:12.637 --> 00:02:14.490
"The massacre might really be a hologram,"

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.570
or an "illusion,"

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.720
that it was "the fakest
thing since the $3 bill,"

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.390
and that other Sandy
Hook families were paid

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.490
to actually fake their loved one's deaths.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.140
Now, the lead plaintiff
in the Connecticut case

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.160
was Erica Lafferty,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.920
the daughter of school principal
Dawn Lafferty Hochsprung,

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.600
who was murdered by the same gunman

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.040
as the Sandy Hook children.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.990
Now, the plaintiffs pleaded
four causes of action

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:34.920
against Jones:

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:35.940
invasion of privacy,

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.260
negligent and intentional infliction

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.370
of emotional distress,

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:41.130
violations of Connecticut
Unfair Practices Act,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.260
CUTPA, C-U-T-P-A,

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.310
and defamation.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.080
Now, the case eventually went to trial,

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.430
but only on damages.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.320
Jones had already lost
the liability phase,

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.730
because of repeated refusals

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.380
to respond to the court's orders,

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.300
and to participate in
the discovery process.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.420
Now, Jones constantly whines
about the legal system,

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.740
and a supposed grand conspiracy

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.080
to deny him the right to due process,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.760
because these whines bring him viewers

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.080
and help him sell supplements

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.700
that are basically just trucker speed.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.520
However, in reality, Jones
wasn't denied due process.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.800
He simply refused to fully defend the case

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.600
and engage in the discovery process,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.220
or listen to the court's orders.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.230
And as we've discussed
many times on this channel,

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:18.210
a SLAPP lawsuit is filed by someone

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.460
in order to silence and intimidate
people for their speech.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.290
And SLAPP suits are genuinely bad,

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:25.380
since they can allow powerful
people to stifle free speech

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.750
simply by draining the
target's financial resources.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.580
And when the Sandy Hook
survivors sued Jones,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.010
he filed motions to dismiss
the plaintiffs' complaints,

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.680
pursuant to Connecticut's
anti-SLAPP statute.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.060
In order to respond to the motions,

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.800
the plaintiffs moved
for limited discovery,

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.330
and Jones opposed it.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.160
Jones and the plaintiffs
went back and forth

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:41.993
for more than a year,

00:03:41.993 --> 00:03:44.460
with Jones usually asking for more time,

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.710
and the court giving him that time.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.330
Eventually, Jones stopped complying

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.010
with the discovery orders entirely,

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.260
even though the court had
agreed to some of his requests

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.300
about limiting the
scope of that discovery.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.100
But finally, in 2021,

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.080
the trial court said
that Jones simply refused

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.610
to comply with the discovery orders.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.590
So Judge Bellis criticized Jones' attorney

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.500
for providing only sanitized,
inaccurate financial records,

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.500
and showed a callous disregard
for her repeated rulings

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.750
to provide complete analytics data.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.457
She found Jones' attorney's
actions were, quote,

00:04:12.457 --> 00:04:13.620
"not just careful,

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.410
but constituted a pattern
of obstructive conduct."

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:18.030
Quote, "Neither the court nor the parties

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:18.900
can expect perfection

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.700
when it comes to the discovery process.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:21.990
What is required, however,

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.820
and what all parties are entitled to,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.350
is fundamental fairness

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:26.790
that the other side produces information

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.100
which is within their knowledge,
possession, and power,

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.260
and that the other side
meets its continuing duty

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.420
to disclose additional and new material."

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.130
And so, when Jones refused,

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:38.100
the judge entered default
judgment against Jones.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.570
A default judgment is a binding judgment

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:40.590
in favor of the other party,

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.300
based on some failure to take action

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.350
by the other party.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.183
In other words,

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.860
the court ruled in favor of
the plaintiffs by default.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.800
But after liability was
established by default,

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.270
the Connecticut case went to trial

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.910
on how much damages Jones had to pay.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.470
Each of the plaintiffs presented evidence

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.790
about what they experienced

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.380
as they listened to Jones lie

00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:59.640
about the Sandy Hook shooting,

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.340
how it impacted their
health, jobs, and lives.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.990
William Sherlock's wife, Mary,

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.600
was a school psychologist
killed at Sandy Hook.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.580
He testified that he was harassed online

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:11.160
by people claiming that
his wife never existed.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.200
People made up conspiracy
theories about Sherlock,

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.840
saying he was involved
with the shooter's father,

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.330
or that he was part of a
shadowing network of financiers

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.190
with a motive to create a hoax.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.500
Robert Parker testified
that less than one day

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.880
after his daughter's murder,

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.820
Jones went on his show and
called Parker an actor.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:27.720
Later that same night,

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:28.860
hateful comments were posted

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.080
to the Facebook memorial page for Emily.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.600
Parker said he removed
Emily's Facebook memorial page

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.650
weeks after the shooting,

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.620
because of the harassment
was just too much to control.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.960
Vicki Soto was a teacher
killed in the attack.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:43.110
Her son said that after President
Obama praised his mother,

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.670
people commented on a Facebook post

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.080
claiming that he wasn't real,

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.010
the family wasn't real,

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.690
and that his mother didn't exist.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:49.950
Plaintiffs in this case argued,

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.120
and the court recognized,

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.430
that Jones intended to
activate his audience.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.680
Not satisfied with just
misinforming the audience,

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.760
Jones urged his viewers

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.190
to investigate the situation on their own.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.470
Millions of people watch
and listen to Infowars,

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:02.303
for some reason,

00:06:02.303 --> 00:06:04.110
and some of them harassed, stalked,

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.850
and targeted the Sandy Hook families

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.530
and first responders.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:08.700
The plaintiffs recounted

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.440
strangers showing up at their homes,

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:11.273
recording them,

00:06:11.273 --> 00:06:12.750
shouting about conspiracy theories.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.250
Mark Braden said that Jones fans

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.410
urinated on his
seven-year-old son's grave,

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.510
even threatening to dig up the coffin.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.160
Hochsprung Lafferty testified

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.380
that people sent rape
threats to her house.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.213
During the litigation,

00:06:23.213 --> 00:06:24.780
Jones also turned his ire on the judge

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:25.950
and the lawyers involved in the case,

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.300
asking his fans to do his dirty work.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.280
He said, quote, "To the
Patriots that are left,

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.870
and 4chan and 8chan,

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.820
and to anybody that's a patriot,

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.020
I'm under attack.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:35.970
If they bring me down,
they'll bring you down.

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:37.590
I just have faith in you.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:38.520
I'm under attack.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:39.900
And I summon the mean war.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.240
I summon all of it against the enemy."

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.610
The FBI concluded that fringe
political conspiracy theories

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.070
very likely motivated
some domestic extremists,

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.810
citing the Pizzagate conspiracy

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.310
and Jones' Sandy Hook lies.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.020
The plaintiffs' legal team told the jury

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.600
that Jones knew the likely
impact of his actions,

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.010
but that he just didn't care.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:56.880
In closing arguments,

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.897
plaintiffs' attorney
Chris Mattei said, quote,

00:06:58.897 --> 00:07:00.570
"When every single one of these families

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:01.410
were drowning in grief,

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.810
Alex Jones put his foot
right on top of them."

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.550
But now we know the end result here.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.320
We have a partial verdict.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.350
The Alex Jones verdict was
only on compensatory damages.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:14.130
The jury awarded plaintiffs
a whopping $965 million,

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.900
and the breakdown is as follows.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.910
36 million to Bill Sherlock,

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:21.217
90 million to former FBI
agent William Aldenberg.

00:07:21.217 --> 00:07:24.150
$55 million to David and Francine Wheeler,

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:26.741
57.6 million and 73.6 million

00:07:26.741 --> 00:07:28.432
to Mark and Jacqueline Bardeney,

00:07:28.432 --> 00:07:31.710
81.6 million and 73.6
million, respectively,

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.277
to Ian and Nicole Hockley,

00:07:33.277 --> 00:07:36.660
$231 million to the
family of slain teacher

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.407
Victoria Leigh Soto,

00:07:38.407 --> 00:07:41.100
$121 million to Robert Parker.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.230
Now, on top of these compensatory damages,

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.100
the judge will determine

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.100
whether Jones owes punitive
damages next month.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:47.933
Now, what's the difference

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:50.040
between punitive and compensatory damages?

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.600
Well, compensatory damages are designed

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.160
to compensate the victim's losses,

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.370
whereas punitive damages are
designed to punish bad actors.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.100
Compensatory damages pay a
plaintiff back for losses.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.500
They cover things like
medical bills, hospital bills,

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.610
future medical expenses,

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.380
and lost pay from missing work.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.540
These damages are generally not capped,

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.610
which is why the verdict was so high.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:09.443
Now, on the other hand,

00:08:09.443 --> 00:08:11.970
states often have caps
on punitive damages.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:12.990
What can I say?

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:16.260
Businesses often lobby to
prevent huge punitive awards,

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.780
because they don't like
paying huge punitive awards.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:20.400
And this is often what's contemplated

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.690
by the term tort reform.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:23.280
And under Connecticut common law,

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.920
courts have the discretion
to award punitive damages

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.900
when the evidence shows
a reckless indifference

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:28.920
to the rights of others,

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.320
or an intentional or wanton
violation of those rights.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.540
This determination is made by the judge.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.190
Common law punitive damages in Connecticut

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:36.990
are limited to the cost of
bringing the litigation,

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.700
including plaintiffs' attorney's fees.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:42.030
However, the Connecticut Unfair
Trade Practices Act claim

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:45.510
opens Jones up to a bigger
punitive damages award.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:46.410
The punitive damages

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:49.140
awarded under the Connecticut
Unfair Trade Practices Act

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:50.550
are not capped.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.040
In order to support an
award of punitive damages

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:54.090
under that act,

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.340
quote, "The evidence must
reveal a reckless indifference

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.180
to the rights of others

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:00.150
or intentional and wanton
violation of those rights."

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.770
A plaintiff doesn't even need to plead

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:03.150
or prove compensatory damages

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.790
in order to recover punitive
damages under the act,

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.280
but since the application of
punitive damages under that act

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:09.113
is so broad,

00:09:09.113 --> 00:09:10.560
the Connecticut Supreme Court has noted

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:13.230
that it creates an essentially
equitable cause of action.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.100
In other words,

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.540
it's very good for the plaintiffs.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:16.373
In Connecticut,

00:09:16.373 --> 00:09:19.020
if jurors find that punitive
damages are appropriate,

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.420
the judge then determines that amount.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:24.330
This will happen at a
separate hearing in November.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.750
Jones characterized his stance
as a boycott of the trial.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.480
Since his lack of compliance
with court rules and procedures

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.960
has resulted in two default
judgments and two big verdicts,

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.300
you might think that he
would change strategies

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.860
for punitive damages,

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.150
but he is, of course, more likely

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.577
to double down on his losing strategy.

00:09:41.577 --> 00:09:44.490
(Alex yells)

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:45.323
Now, so far,

00:09:45.323 --> 00:09:47.340
all the money awarded to the
plaintiffs in the Jones case

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.810
is for compensatory damages.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.000
And although Jones will certainly appeal,

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.490
judges are often reluctant
to reduce a jury award,

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.720
especially in a state like Connecticut,

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.510
which has no caps on compensatory damages.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:00.780
So it's possible that the awards
will be reduced on appeal,

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.640
but they won't be automatically reduced,

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:05.130
as punitive damages often are.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.630
Now, I should also note that, often,

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:09.570
juries are not told about
limits on punitive damages,

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.450
so they don't shift what would
normally be a punitive damage

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.730
into a compensatory damage award.

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:16.050
And some have speculated here

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:19.140
that following along the limits in Texas

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.100
on punitive damages,

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.750
it's possible that this jury

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:24.000
overloaded the compensatory damages

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.590
in this particular case.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:26.423
But at the moment,

00:10:26.423 --> 00:10:27.256
there's no way to know.

00:10:27.256 --> 00:10:28.950
Juries are a black box.

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:30.690
Now, Jones also complicated his appeal

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.450
by refusing to put on a
defense in the damages phase.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:34.980
He could have called his own witnesses

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.150
and testified himself,

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.380
like he did in Texas.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.390
By doing so, there would've
been evidence on the record

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:41.370
showing why the damages
should have been lower,

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.660
and the jury could have considered

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.490
whether Jones was contrite,

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.260
whether he made a formal apology,

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:47.730
whether he did the things to ensure

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:49.380
that the Infowars contributors

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:52.320
won't make crazy claims
like this in the future.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:54.570
But since he did not
put on his own evidence,

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.940
the appeal is gonna be
less straightforward.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.200
Now, as for mitigating factors,

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.490
Jones has not helped his case

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:00.360
by going on his show

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.640
and stating that the lawsuits
are trying to stop him

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.310
from talking about Parkland and Uvalde.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.870
Alex Jones is suggesting

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.700
that maybe there's a conspiracy going on

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.250
in those two horrific mass shootings.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.210
Now, this kind of rhetoric

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:14.490
is probably not gonna help
him show that he's sorry,

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:15.540
that he's learned his lesson,

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:17.580
or any of the things he
half-heartedly argued

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.050
in the Texas case.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.730
The bigger question that
everyone wants to know

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:22.680
is will the plaintiffs ever get paid?

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:25.530
Jones says he only has about
$2 million to his name,

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.300
yet Jones raised millions of dollars

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:29.340
after the Texas verdict came out.

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:31.110
Experts testified that Infowars

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:33.990
is between 100 and $250 million,

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:36.120
and plaintiffs' lawyers
promised to chase Jones

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:36.953
to the end of the year,

00:11:36.953 --> 00:11:38.310
to collect on the judgment.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:39.810
So how will they do that?

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:41.910
Well, lawyers will have to connect Jones

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.890
to the many shell
companies that he's set up

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:46.560
for Infowars and his
associated businesses.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:47.550
They'll probably argue

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:50.373
that even though these entities
are corporations and LLCs,

00:11:50.373 --> 00:11:53.400
that the companies and Jones
are legally the same entity,

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.890
and the corporate veil should be pierced.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:57.330
If that eventually happens,

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.460
Jones' personal assets could be seized

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:00.900
as well as the corporate assets.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.090
Now, all of this implicates
the bankruptcy court, too.

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.320
As we've discussed before,

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.153
Jones and his companies

00:12:05.153 --> 00:12:06.930
have filed for bankruptcy protection,

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.940
but Jones has suffered some setbacks.

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:10.650
A bankruptcy judge removed the lawyer

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:13.050
and chief restructuring officer
for Free Speech Systems,

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:15.060
the parent company of Infowars,

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:18.540
after they failed to disclose
prior connections to Jones.

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:20.280
The judge also directed
the bankruptcy trustee

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.560
to examine Free Speech
Systems' financial affairs,

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.930
operations, and insider relationships.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.330
This happened after creditors
complained to the court

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:28.770
that the company was hiding its assets

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.750
through complex corporate structures.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.420
As I discussed in my last Jones video,

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:37.560
a company owned by Jones's
parents, PQPR Holdings,

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.770
says it's a major creditor
of Free Speech Systems.

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:44.784
Jones allegedly owes
Mom and Pop $54 million.

00:12:44.784 --> 00:12:46.290
But the bankruptcy judge found

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.330
that there has been,
quote, "a lack of candor"

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.950
by the companies and their lawyers,

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.480
and this means that the bankruptcy case

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.550
is already traveling the same path

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.920
as the Texas and Connecticut lawsuits.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.450
Now, Liz Dye is a fantastic journalist

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.160
who has been following
the Jones bankruptcy,

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.810
where most of the action
is likely to take place

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:01.650
in the future.

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:03.870
Yes, she is a complete masochist.

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:04.950
So let's ask her.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.860
Liz, what effect is this
verdict likely to have

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:09.840
on the rest of the bankruptcies?

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.970
- Yesterday, Jones promised his viewers

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:13.740
that they could shower him with cash,

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:15.300
and not have to worry
that any of the money

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.190
would go to the Sandy Hook victims.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.280
The reality is that his
company, FSS, is in bankruptcy

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.860
and he doesn't really have
control over it anymore.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:25.410
And because Alex Jones is Alex Jones,

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.060
he's done a bunch of really shady things

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:28.590
that mean he has even less control

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:30.840
than a normal debtor would in bankruptcy.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:32.460
The most egregious thing he did

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:35.100
was to have the company
sign two promissory notes

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:36.540
for upwards of $50 million

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.390
right around the time
that he got defaulted

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:41.010
in the Sandy Hook cases.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:43.920
So, suddenly, the company
which supplies his beet juice

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.410
and male vitality pills remembered

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:50.310
that it hadn't billed FSS for
years for products supplied,

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:54.240
and so FSS owed the drug
supplier $50 million,

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:55.530
at least in theory.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:58.560
So, in 2021, FSS signed these two notes,

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:01.140
and started shoveling
mountains of cash out the door

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:03.000
to the drug supply company.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.560
The effect of the notes

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:07.050
is to make the drug supply company

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:09.000
first in line to get paid.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.950
But it turns out that
the supplement company

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.560
is owned, in whole, by
Jones and his parents

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.600
through a series of Nevada LLCs.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.600
So what he's done is
effectively impoverished FSS,

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:21.390
and claimed all of its assets
for himself personally,

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:23.490
which is pretty convenient.

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:25.530
Months ago, the Texas plaintiff sued,

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.360
saying that the notes
were fraudulent transfers

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.800
and also alleging that Jones

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:31.320
had made a lot of cash
transfers to himself

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:32.880
from the company coffers.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:33.990
So the bankruptcy court

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:36.510
is looking both at the promissory notes

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:38.190
and at those cash transfers,

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.080
to see if they should be clawed back.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.510
So how much the plaintiffs get paid, here,

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:45.900
really depends on whether the
court tosses out the notes

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:48.450
and claws back that
cash from Jones himself.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.370
Secondarily, Jones claims the right

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:53.130
to have FSS indemnify
him for any jury verdict,

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.650
which would mean that he's
not on the hook, personally,

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:58.110
for any of the money
owed to these plaintiffs.

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:00.120
And that would be cool for him,

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.950
because he could loot the company,

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:06.090
claim all of its assets were
owed to him, personally,

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.460
and then, free from
any personal liability,

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:10.410
he can go and do the same
thing somewhere else.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.300
So he can start Shminfowars,

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.940
and sell male vitality pills there,

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:17.400
using the same shtick that he uses here.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.830
So there are a lot of moving
parts in this bankruptcy,

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.360
and I think that's
where most of the action

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:22.590
is gonna wind up.

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:23.430
- Yes, at this point,

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:25.740
Shminfowars sounds more reputable

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.090
than the original Infowars.

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.340
Definitely give Liz a follow on Twitter.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:31.710
Now, Alex Jones isn't
personally in bankruptcy yet.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:32.880
It's going to be a fight,

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.860
but his personal assets
are likely to be subject

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.300
to this giant award.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:38.940
And I should probably make
